<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Dragsa entitlements (macOS).

    hardenedRuntime is OFF in electron-builder (deliberate — no codesign identity,
    no notarization). These entitlements are therefore not enforced by the
    kernel; they exist so that flipping hardenedRuntime: true later (if we ever
    acquire a Developer ID) only requires a config change, not a plist edit.

    The minimum Dragsa needs from a hardened runtime:
      • com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory — V8 JIT
      • com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit — V8 JIT (paired with the above on
        recent macOS)
      • com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation — for the bundled
        PyInstaller MCP binary, which links against system Python framework
        bits that aren't individually signed
      • com.apple.security.network.client — Electron fetches the brain over
        HTTPS, MCP dials the brain WSS endpoint
      • com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write — file save/open
        dialogs (e.g. report downloads initiated from the renderer)

    Nothing else is required: no app sandbox, no iCloud, no push, no
    microphone, no camera, no location.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>